# Dependencies
#
# This is the guardrail for the plugin's core design property: it must ship NO
# dependencies, so that the host's pi-ai is the only pi-ai on the machine.
# If a node_modules/ ever appeared in the repository, a fresh
# `dsh plugin add` would install a vendored second copy of @earendil-works/pi-ai,
# which is exactly the pi-ai generation mismatch that breaks
# dsh-workbuddy-xdpool (see README).
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Logs and debug output
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Local environment and credentials — never commit these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# Test and build scratch
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
dist/
